  "details": "If you have an object with a parent (or other) constraint on it, and you have an animation that changes the transform of that object, the physbones positions are not updated in-game. \n\nAnnoyingly it works fine in the editor but not in game. It also works fine if you do not animate the bones, in that case the physbones will follow their constrained position as intended.\n \nIn game the bones appear to animate normally, but if you bring up the debug overlay, the physbones are still in their animated position, and can be bapped/grabbed/etc. from that position. (The physbones are basically ignoring the constraint). This happens regardless of whether or not the physbone has \"Is Animated\" enabled.\n\nVRCSDK3-AVATAR-2022.07.26.21.45_Public\nClient Build 1221\n\nEdit 1: ------------------------------------\nWith further testing I've found even having an animation that animates those bones anywhere at all, even if the layer weight is down, still prevents the physbones from following constraints in game.\n\nEdit 2: ------------------------------------\nTrying to debug this I've determined that this is an issue if any parents of the physbone in the hierarchy have animation constraints and are also animated, the mesh/gameobjects will follow the constraints, but the physbones (as visible in the debug overlay) will follow the animation.",
